    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31674" root="غرس" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْرِسٌ</span></b>  <i>A place of planting:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغَارِسُ</span>. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Hence, metaphorically, (tropical:)  <i>A woman,</i> or <i>wife.</i>
(Har p. 502.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [Hence also the saying,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُطْلُبِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الخَيْرَ فِى مَغَارِسِهِ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>Seek thou good in the persons
in whom it is naturally implanted</i>]; as also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغَارِزِهِ</span>. (A and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غرز</span>.)

